        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c6a569f2-1ae1-5400-bd36-3dadbfe35e0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marlon Brando, Joseph L. Mankiewicz, John Houseman, William Shakespeare\n- Works: Julius Caesar, The Wild One, Guys and Dolls, Sayonara, Last Tango in Paris, Apocalypse Now\n- Topics: Acting careers, Film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Marlon Brando Jr. was born on April 3, 1924, and he was an American actor, film director, and political activist.\n- Julius Caesar is a 1953 epic Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer film adaptation of William Shakespeare’s play Julius Caesar.\n- Joseph L. Mankiewicz directed Julius Caesar and wrote its uncredited screenplay.\n- John Houseman produced Julius Caesar.\n- Marlon Brando appeared in Julius Caesar (1953), The Wild One (1953), Guys and Dolls (1955), Sayonara (1957), Last Tango in Paris (1972), and Apocalypse Now (1979).\n- Marlon Brando Jr. died on July 1, 2004.",
